AGENTS.md
**/AGENTS.md
z_history/
**/z_history/
**/scenario.json.bak
**/_scratch/
**/.pytest_cache/
tests/node_modules/
tests/test-results/
tests/playwright-report/
.DS_Store
# cinemagraph raw pre-loop clips — kept locally so a loop can be switched (boomerang↔crossfade) without
# re-generating; the player never needs them, so don't push them to the public site.
**/*_raw.mp4
**/*.reloop.mp4
# pre-edit cinemagraph originals (the picked/played clip keeps the plain name)
**/*_orig.mp4
# seam-repair undo snapshots — every gradient/AI seam fix drops one beside the image it repaired, and
# they MUST stay on disk (that is what the hub's Undo reads). The player never fetches them. 19 of these
# were sitting in Egypt alone at its audit (2026-08-28).
**/*_undo*.png
# the world plate — the shared continuity REFERENCE the art pipeline feeds to gpt-image, shown in the
# console's World-plate panel. Authoring-only: it is never fetched at play time, but it must stay on disk
# (moving it breaks both the panel and the generation reference), so ignore it rather than archiving it.
**/_world/

# --- Keep the public repo to PLAY-REQUIRED assets only (2026-08-06) ---
# Rule: only files the player fetches at runtime (scenario.json, play.html, referenced
# panoramas/cinemagraphs/audio/images, data CSVs, shared engine, decoder) belong on the
# public site. Authoring records, build caches, backups, and history-tier dirs do not.
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT untrack already-committed files — after this syncs to the Mac,
# run once in the escape_rooms repo:  git rm -r --cached . && git add . && git commit
# (re-applies these rules; disk files are untouched, git just stops tracking the ignored ones.)

# Design records + authoring docs (root/**/AGENTS.md already ignored above)
**/notes.md
**/wiring_checklist.md
# the vetted landing-story snapshot validate_story.py diffs against — authoring only
**/.vetted_story.txt
# All backup / pre-edit snapshots (broadens the scenario.json.bak line above)
**/*.bak
**/scenario.json.pre_*
# Python build/test caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# ALL history-tier archive dirs (the z_ convention), not just z_history/
z_*/
**/z_*/


# --- Cinemagraph R&D bench — authoring-only (2026-08-31) ---
# authoring_v2/ui/cine360/ is the 360-cinemagraph parameter-sweep bench: ~325 experiment clips,
# 2.1 GB, several over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. No scenario.json references it. It wedged a
# push once; githooks/pre-push now catches that class. Ignore the media AND the bench pages.
authoring_v2/ui/cine360/
authoring_v2/ui/cine360_*.html

# Timestamped / suffixed backups — `**/*.bak` above does NOT match `*.bak_20260830_0748`,
# `*.bak_flash_1022`, `*.bak_20260828` etc., which is how four cine360_test snapshots and a
# scenario.json backup reached the same commit.
**/*.bak_*
**/*.pre_*

# Authoring records + scratch (canon: only play-required files reach public GitHub)
notes/
temp/
